# Portfolio versions

## v1.0 = the full original production site

When the user says **v1.0**, **v1**, or **the old site**, they mean the complete original portfolio — original home plus every existing case study and note. Not a partial or restyled stand-in.

- Frozen as git tag `v1.0` on commit `e5ce338`
- Route: `/v1` → `PortfolioHome` (name/logo stays on `/v1`)
- If they ask to “give me v1.0” or switch back, restore that full original experience

## v2.0 = the new UI

When the user says **v2.0**, **v2**, or **the new UI**, they mean the redesigned homepage and any new UI that follows. Home shipped first; project pages get rebuilt one by one. Until a case study is rebuilt, keep using the existing production project/note pages.

- Route: `/` → `PortfolioHomeV2`
- Case study / note “back” links go to `/` (the v2 home)
- Work continues on branch `v2`
- Do not merge to `main` or deploy unless the user explicitly says to go live

## Production

Live site deploys from `main` via Vercel: https://github.com/monicaaddepalli/portfolio.git

- `/` — v2.0 home
- `/v1` — full v1.0 home
- `/work/*` and `/notes/*` — existing production case studies and notes

## Local

- v2 home: http://localhost:5173/
- v1 home: http://localhost:5173/v1
